From 2a23af3faa612b85c986d028768b38328bd04c18 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 15:58:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/18] BananaDS perf: at 2x the output stage writes straight
 into the rows (render.2d_emit_zip)

EmitA at 2x converted each of a 3D line's four composited quarters into a 256-pixel line of its own (WriteLine:
master brightness, 6-to-8-bit expansion; 240k instructions a frame on the 2D thread on dsstress L5) and then
zipped the lines' even and odd pixels into the frame's two 512-pixel rows (164k); EmitB, and EmitA for a line
without the 3D layer, converted the line and then doubled it into its two rows (DoubleLine; EmitB 130k).
WriteZipNeon and WriteDoubleNeon do each in one pass: WriteLineNeon's planes, zipped byte by byte (output pixel
2i is even pixel i, 2i + 1 odd pixel i) or with each byte twice, stored once; no line in between. Exact: a random
test against WriteLineNeon + ZipLine / DoubleLine over every brightness mode and factor, 6000 cases, 0 mismatches
(perf evidence, zip_test.cpp). Display modes 0, 2 and 3 go as before. render.2d_emit_zip=off keeps the two passes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PvbFhKAw3ERk5a13S651g1
